    {
      "id": "about",
      "type": "layout.comment",
      "name": "Original distortion fixtures - MIT",
      "description": "Original 16-bit RGB target, fixture equations, references and project under the repository's MIT license. Four branches generate shear, perspective, lens-like and seeded distortions, then reuse their typed maps through ordinary Remap blocks. Each comparison must have zero maximum pixel error. Truth maps are output-to-input sampling coordinates, not estimated registration or a guessed forward transform. Probes and effective coefficients are in assets/truth.json. Validity excludes source borders and selections conservatively for interpolation support. Fixed-point maps can introduce extra quantization; float64 cubic remap is rejected because the pinned native build corrupts boundary samples. This is a synthetic stress model, not a camera calibration. API: https://docs.opencv.org/5.0/main_modules/imgproc_transform.html",
      "parameters": {},
      "position": [
